---
// The single idea to keep, if you keep one: the sound OF something, not FOR it.
// Full-bleed night block over svhgpt-04 (a seated figure radiating sound), with
// a two-card contrast and a closing pull. Shared by everyone; the mode tag just
// reframes who it's addressed to.
---

<section class="wn-core">
  <div class="wn-core-bg" data-parallax data-parallax-speed="0.16" aria-hidden="true">
    <img src="/media/library/svhgpt-04-sound-of-not-for.webp" alt="" />
  </div>
  <div class="wn-core-inner">
    <div class="wn-mode-tag wn-reveal">
      The distinction that matters most
      <span class="wn-mode-chip" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="wn-core-head wn-reveal">
      Make the sound <em>of</em> something —<br />not the sound <em>for</em> it.
    </h2>

    <div class="wn-core-pair">
      <div class="wn-core-card wn-reveal">
        <div class="wn-core-kicker">Sound healing — sound FOR you</div>
        <h4>Something comes in from outside</h4>
        <p>
          Someone plays the bowls, or sings over you, and you lie there and
          receive it. The older idea: something external comes in and changes
          you, like taking a pill.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wn-core-card wn-core-card--of wn-reveal" style="--wn-delay: 120ms">
        <div class="wn-core-kicker">Somatic Vocal Healing — sound OF you</div>
        <h4>You give your own state a voice</h4>
        <p>
          You make the sound <em>of</em> your tiredness, <em>of</em> the tightness in
          your chest, <em>of</em> the grief that's sat there a week. The healing is in
          the acknowledgment — in being present <em>with</em> the thing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="wn-core-pull wn-reveal">
      When something is truly met, it stops needing to clamour.
      <em>It loses its reason to keep shouting.</em>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
